          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Educational Contributions</strong><br>\nConfucius's contributions to education are notable. He was one of the first to advocate for the education of the common people, not just the elite. He believed that education was a means to cultivate virtue and that a virtuous populace was necessary for a stable and prosperous state.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Political Views</strong><br>\nConfucius held specific views on politics, emphasizing the role of benevolent leadership. He taught that a ruler should lead by example and inspire moral virtues in his subjects. According to Confucius, good governance relied on the ruler's moral character rather than on strict laws and punishments.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and Modern Relevance</strong><br>\nConfucius's legacy remains influential in the modern world. His thoughts on respect, education, and governance continue to be relevant and are often cited in discussions on ethics and leadership. As China emerges as a global power, there is renewed interest in Confucian values as a guiding philosophy for personal conduct and public policy.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
